WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.050
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:07.290
<i>Last week on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>...</i>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.660
<i>There are limits to what a family 
of kids can do on their own.</i>

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:20.120
<i>That's why I went out to meet my old tutor,
 hoping that she might help us out.</i>

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:25.330
<i>But when I met her, she had 
no intention of helping me.</i>

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.670
<i>She was just angry about my old 
dismissiveness towards her.</i>

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.310
<i>Suishi-neesan came along and helped me out,</i>

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.770
<i>but I was pretty depressed about being 
resented by someone I thought I could trust.</i>

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:51.030
<i>But on the way home, I ran into Sumire-chan, 
whose innocence reassured me a little.</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.120
<b>#4: Homing</b>

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.970
Oh, dear me! What's all this?

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.850
Darling, it seems our little 
love nest is finished.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.690
Don't worry, honey. 
I've already taken measures.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.790
Though I hope penitentiary food
 is a little better than this...

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.050
What shall we do with the children?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.610
A fine question.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.220
A very fine question...

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.780
What's going on?

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.960
What's with all the noise 
in the middle of the night?

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.130
Take this.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.470
Now, pay attention! Your mother and I...

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.100
...are going to leave for a little while.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:36.950
What?

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.650
You all have to move out, too.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.160
Be good boys and girls until we come for you.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.920
Tanisu. Take care of the others.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.510
I've stored all the data in the 
usual place. Take care of the rest.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.080
The password is...

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.010
Snow, you'll want to stay
 a dog for a while, all right?

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.740
It's as I told you before.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:16.090
You'll be the one who completes our research.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:23.780
<i>After they finished talking, 
Mom and Dad had us wait in the lab.</i>

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.770
<i>Not long after, the institute blew up.</i>

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.910
<i>We managed to get to the opposite shore,</i>

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.780
<i>but the police found us right away.</i>

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.510
<i>Our parents had been arrested, 
and we had no relatives,</i>

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.140
<i>so the government went through 
a a social welfare service</i>

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.870
<i>to find us a new home.</i>

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.720
<i>We thought we'd have to wait a long time.</i>

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.930
<i>We never thought someone would 
make an offer so quickly.</i>

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:59.030
<i>My sisters... Well, they <i>looked</i> 
human for the time being,</i>

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:03.150
<i>but the entire time between the police 
finding us and us being taken to our new home,</i>

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.240
<i>we were worried about when the 
medicine might lose effect.</i>

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.290
<i>We were lucky that it only lost 
effect after everyone left...</i>

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.750
<i>But that's when the side effects occurred...</i>

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.870
<i>Of course, it would be best not to 
have to use the medicine at all.</i>

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:34.950
<i>But to do that...</i>

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.210
I heard a sound downstairs.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:42.500
Let's check it out together.

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.560
What's all the fuss at this hour?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.830
Oh, sorry. We're fine.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.330
Who could it be at this hour?

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.800
Hello? Oh, yes!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.800
Is that so?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.820
Okay, got it.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.140
Who was it?

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.810
The landlord's coming home tomorrow.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.810
Landlord?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.320
The guy who owns this house.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.850
Who is he?

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.170
I've never met him, so I don't know,

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:31.270
but he sounded really normal over the phone.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.180
You've got bugs.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.750
Don't eat them!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.750
If a normal person were to see all of this...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.770
Let's go, puppy!

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.440
We're finished.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.500
We don't have much medicine left.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.720
Which means...

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.340
Listen, everyone!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.050
Let's go back to the lab!

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.720
There must be more medicine there...

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.480
And... the research data, too!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.290
Oh, hooray!

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.240
When are we heading out?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.860
Well, early tomorrow, I hope...

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.000
Yes! We're going home!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.090
Oh, could I bring my new clothing?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.650
We're just picking up 
some stuff we left there.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.960
We won't need to change clothes.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.530
We can't go back to our old lives.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.190
Why?

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:33.050
I don't know how to get this across,

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.960
but this is the answer.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.610
Tanisu...

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.940
Don't you threaten us with 
that crap, you damn brat!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.440
I'm not trying to threaten you.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:49.270
Meeting my tutor made it really clear.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:53.090
If we want to keep hiding
 the fact that you're modified,

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:56.950
and if we want you to avoid 
the terrible side effects this has,

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.450
then I have to keep researching the medicine!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:04.980
I don't want you guys to 
suffer like that again.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.070
I don't want to take the medicine.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.920
Neither do I...

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:15.610
If I can finish the research, 
we can stave off the side e—

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:17.200
<b>Genius</b>

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.610
What happened to the 
makeup plan from before?!

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:20.990
It ain't like I'm that desperate 
to go outside, anyway!

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.140
That's just a temporary fix!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.740
And if the landlord shows up, 
he'll definitely realize something's off!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.490
Ashisu, Aisuri.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.460
Do you remember when Tanisu 
fixed up that TV we found?

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.920
That was super cool!

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.360
The people inside it seemed 
to be having so much fun!

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:42.000
Yeah, yeah!

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.750
If you gain human forms, 
you can do the same things.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.540
We can eat the legendary 108-dish 
Chinese food full course?!

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:54.620
I can dive into the sea and look at 
fish, and slide along that white sand?

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.380
I can ride the bullet train, climb mountains, 
and watch 3D movies?!

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.000
I can ride airplanes, too!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.680
Go, go! Tanisu!

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.610
We're behind you, Tanisu!

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.960
Great job, Snow-niisan.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.560
Do you want to go outside too, Snow-niisan?

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:14.190
Well, I suppose that I would.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.200
But being with you all is all I need.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.860
Snow-niisan...

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.410
I'm sure your wishes will 
all come true some day.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.040
Tomorrow morning, we're heading out.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.110
Huh? You were all waiting for me here?

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:42.150
You're really freakin' late. What time is it?

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.300
One o'clock.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.270
I didn't know book stores 
only opened at 10...

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.740
I bought some food, too. Here.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.360
Yeah!

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.360
Cool!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.090
I was doing a lot of research 
with Suishi-neesan.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.690
Here's a map.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.890
This is the island we're on now.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:00.250
It's not too far to the lab.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.950
If we leave from this beach,

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.330
we should arrive in 30 minutes by boat.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.800
That's the plan, so let's head out!

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.360
Tanisu.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.300
I went with you this morning, 
so I can't go with you now.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.240
Got it.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.490
Careful on your way home, okay?

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.730
You see that island?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:45.900
That's where our house is.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.920
Let's get ready.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.830
Why are you getting changed?

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:56.940
I thought it might heighten 
the feel of adventure!

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.800
Then why the lab coat?

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.680
It's the only way I feel comfortable!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.760
You make it too easy to tease you.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.610
<i>Why did Mom and Dad devote 
themselves to that research?</i>

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.600
<i>Was it just to satisfy 
a hunger for knowledge?</i>

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.820
Yeah!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:21.450
<i>What's the point of having me
 continue their research?</i>

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:21.770
Let's go!

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:24.320
<i>There might be an answer in the data.</i>

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:30.080
If you two get tired, you can climb back on.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.800
Tanisu still has the key.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:45.990
I saw it in a newspaper, 
but the institute is sealed off now.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.790
There are apparently a lot 
of government people inside,

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.450
so we need to make sure 
we're not seen sneaking in.

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:55.270
You guys know the shortcuts 
through the forest really well,

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.740
so I'll count on you to guide me.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:57.860
Roger!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.820
Puppy, you be on the look-out 
for anyone suspicious, okay?

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.780
Wait for me!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.330
So cute!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.580
Can I eat it?

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:14.710
Over there!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.720
It felt like a longer walk before.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.330
It's because you always got lost.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.730
Now that I'm used to the houses 
outside, the old lab feels so...

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.210
So cool!

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:36.700
Can I take that thing back with me?

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.230
No!

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.440
There's no one inside, either.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.660
Upsy-daisy!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.990
It's open here.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:53.480
Okay...

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.670
The camera's not working.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:04.630
Okay!

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:06.840
Sorry for the wait.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.140
It's fine!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.640
You're not going?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.340
Hold on. Puppy,

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:17.540
can you tell how many people 
are inside the building by smell?

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:22.150
Let's go to the kitchen first, then.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.150
Are you hungry?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.530
If the cameras aren't working,

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.890
the control room next to
 the kitchen isn't, either.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:33.030
If we can get there first and get 
the security monitors working,

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:36.040
we can get an idea of what's 
going on in the building.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.140
Wow!

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.640
It's just like a Hollywood movie!

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.140
You were hiding this great place from us!

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.650
I was hoping to avoid any damage.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.410
It's just a bunch of monitors.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:05.150
How would I get damaged here?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.660
I wasn't talking about damage to <i>you</i>...

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.860
What's with the password 
that unlocked it, too?

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.670
Just a peek!

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.160
It's not like I thought it up...

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:20.640
Dad said this was to monitor guests.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:23.480
I know. There might be old recordings.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:24.580
Where?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.650
No, they're all gone.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.050
I wonder if there's another 
way to get at the data.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.730
You guys are good at tag, right?

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:35.680
Yeah!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.210
Find us a good way out, okay?

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:38.690
Leave it to us!

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:38.690
Understood!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:30.960
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.560
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.960
<i>Today's theme is...</i>

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.960
<b>Today's theme is...</b>

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:31.820
<b>Headquarters</b>

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.590
<b>This time...</b>

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.410
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.410
<b>We see where the 
comics are published</b>

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:42.500
<b>Shinchosha's Monthly Comic 
Bunch Editorial Department!</b>

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:47.610
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:47.610
<b>Chief Editor  Uotani Ryota-san</b>

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.610
<b>How did you end up publishing 
<i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:55.150
Japanese manga is very popular overseas.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:59.340
Lately, the trend of foreign writers 
wanting to make their debut in Japan

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:00.830
has been getting much stronger.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.340
We ended up publishing <i>Frankenstein Family</i> 
after someone in the publishing department

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.720
over there talked with us 
at a manga-related event

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:13.670
and showed us ten comics currently 
popular in China and Taiwan.

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.980
Out of those, I thought <i>Frankenstein 
Family</i> might do well in Japan.

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:20.680
And so we published it.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:26.940
As the title suggests, "Family" is 
a big theme of <i>Frankenstein Family</i>.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:31.150
"Family" is a universal theme wherever 
you go, be it China, Taiwan, or Japan.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:37.410
I thought it would cross the cultural 
barriers and reach the readers.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:43.400
The concept is novel and the 
characters are funny and charming.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:45.540
That made me really want to publish it.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.540
<b>How does publishing a foreign
 manga change the usual process?</b>

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:54.030
Of course, the original isn't in Japanese, 
so we have to hire a translator.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:59.040
But there are a lot of phrases that sound
 strange in Japanese if translated directly,

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.200
or that just won't sound colloquial.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.120
It creates discrepancies 
between the intended meaning

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.460
and what the readers end up hearing.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.900
Those sorts of quiet misunderstandings 
are really hard to avoid.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:14.810
Fortunately, the writer, Yanai-sensei, 
is very good at Japanese,

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:20.690
so if we're not sure, we can 
ask what we should do.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.240
I think that's really great.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.880
There are also places with drawn lettering.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:31.330
Not the text written with a computer,

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:35.840
but places where the artist 
has drawn in the words.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:39.800
We need to adjust those, and that 
takes a while, but that's all.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:42.390
I don't think there were any major problems.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.930
<b>How do the readers like it?</b>

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.870
Well, when it was first being published,

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:56.100
they had already decided to make 
a TV anime for it in Japan.

00:18:56.100 --> 00:19:00.530
And a lot of people were 
really hoping for an anime.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:04.250
Now on Comic Bunch Web, 
our official home page,

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.160
we've got a PV and stuff,

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.210
and I see that the views on it are very good.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:15.530
It makes me think people really 
want that anime adaptation.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.130
<b>We asked Uotani-san our questions, too!</b>

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:22.630
<b>If you were going to be modified, 
what power would you want?</b>

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:24.120
I see.

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.690
Good question.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:36.720
The character Snow is a dog-human 
hybrid. He can become a dog.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.920
I'd like to become a cat, I think.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.720
They're so laid-back.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.570
I'd like to live a life like that.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.760
I've always liked cats, too.

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.300
Back to Snow.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:54.250
Getting to see people and 
society from his point of view,

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.030
I feel like there's a lot 
you could learn that way.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.800
<b>Let's keep asking! What other 
powers would you want?</b>

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.760
I'm not sure.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:08.430
Maybe the ability to get eight 
hours of sleep in just 30 minutes.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:11.270
That ability would be great.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.860
Let's see...

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:14.490
What else...

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:17.450
Ah...

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:22.280
Teleportation would be great.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:30.120
Because I'm a comics editor, and I don't 
really get a lot of time for vacations.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:34.960
If I could teleport, I could visit all 
the places overseas that I want to see.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.410
If I could do that, I'd use it a lot.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:41.480
<b>Who's your favorite <i>Frankenstein Family</i> character?</b>

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.760
Snow, I think.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:49.930
The concept of the show is kind of hardcore,

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:54.080
with these children being 
modified by their parents.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:57.680
But the characters themselves 
are all so sweet.

00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:02.440
They can't even tell good from evil, really.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:05.580
It's such a shock when you 
see them in the real world.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.250
Part of you thinks, "Will they be okay?"

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:11.910
That really comes through.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:15.580
Out of those, Snow is the big brother,

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:23.160
so I think he represents the highest 
ideal of what you want a family to be.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:29.260
If something happens, 
if someone's in trouble,

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:33.240
Snow-niisan can settle it with a single word.

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:39.730
And in the anime, the voice actor's 
performance really brings out that tolerance.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.800
And his dog form is also really cute.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:45.140
Snow-niisan is definitely my favorite.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:55.160
Thanks, Snow-niisan.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.900
Do you think something happened to him?

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.500
You all stay here. I'll find him.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:07.770
My dog side doesn't handle 
this atmosphere well,

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:10.090
and I've always wanted to try chopsticks...

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:13.100
<b>The first volume of the comic is out, right?</b>

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:18.780
<i>Frankenstein Family</i> is an 
unusual case in Japan, I think.

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:23.110
The anime and the comic 
both debuted the same day.

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:26.790
The fact that you can watch the anime 
the same day the comic comes out...

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:31.700
It's kind of an experiment, in its own way.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:37.530
The comics have a newly-drawn cover, 
different from the Taiwanese version.

00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:42.790
There's also some new mini-comics you can 
only read here and some fold-out pages.

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:47.790
So I think you'll want to pick 
it up to read all the extras.

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:53.320
We also have a really impressive 
cast for the anime,

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:55.800
and if you buy the comic, 
you'll get a lottery ticket,

00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:58.790
that could earn you voice actor autographs,

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:02.180
copies of the script 
autographed by the full cast.

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:07.820
So if you want a chance to win, make 
sure to check out the comics, too.

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.320
<i>Avoiding security,</i>

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.870
<i>we return with the medicine.</i>

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:18.790
<i>It's exciting, sort of like a spy movie...</i>

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:21.130
<i>Actually sneaking around is rough, though.</i>

00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:24.020
<i>But I'm a genius, remember?</i>

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.960
<i>I'll think our way out of this!</i>

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.340
<i>Hey, Niisan!</i>

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:31.540
<i>Don't run away just because 
there's lightning!</i>

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:35.520
<i>Next time on </i>Frankenstein 
Family<i>: "Infiltration."</i>

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>#4:  Infiltration</b>

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:36.600
<i>Catch it, okay?</i>
